From ad9e57f1047abe097dc2593a3683d5f37e395349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yang <473784533@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:58:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AI_EMBED: batch table-scan rows into one request, map answers
 by index

An eval_batch_func_ is registered when the content argument is row-varying, so a vectorized scan
sends up to 64 inputs per request instead of one request per row. Rows the single-row semantics
reject (NULL, empty model id, non-positive dimension) stay on that path, a chunk is only built
from rows that share the model and the dimension, and a service that cannot answer a multi-input
body falls back to one request per row. parse_output now places each returned vector through the
provider's own index label instead of trusting arrival order.

Verified on the built binary (c444c661...): ai_function_enhancement 101/101 and ai_prompt 250/250
line for line against their recorded r/mysql/*.result, plus 10/10 checks of a probe whose mock
reverses the answer list, answers a 64-input request with a single vector, and has a dead port.
---
